 "letterboxd-review-1556010419": {
  "guid": "letterboxd-review-1556010419",
  "title": "Moon Garden",
  "year": 2022,
  "rating": 4.5,
  "like": true,
  "rewatch": false,
  "watched": "2026-10-26",
  "tmdb": 977000,
  "url": "https://letterboxd.com/georgecarmi/film/moon-garden/",
  "review": "rattled me in ways I really wasn't expecting. just an insane plunge into this dark surrealist fairytale pulled straight out of a fucking nightmare. there's something so fascinating about being trapped inside a child's imagination. it's something that carries a lot of familiarity, which you can see through emma's confidence in her exploration of this world, but simultaneously something so deeply unsettling. the logic of dreams is ridiculous and this films embrace of that unknown is quite unnerving. it's not really a straightforward story, there's a lot of ambiguity in this dark adventure, and it more so makes you feel like you've just wandered into some forgotten, twisted fairytale. it's a very special movie in all its strange and experimental creativity, with practical effects I cannot believe aren't talked about regularly as being an insane achievement in this decade of film. every creature, every texture, every environment has this really sincere handmade and decaying quality to it. it's so lovely and so fucked."
 },
